# Bundle digests are taken over FILE BYTES: a charter, a policy table, a
# manifest entry. Git's Windows default (core.autocrlf=true) would check
# those out with CRLF, so the same bundle would compile to a different
# digest on a different operating system — and a run's pin would stop
# meaning one thing. Normalise every text file to LF in the working
# tree, on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets are never normalised.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary
